info[_postman_id]=4172eede-4afb-4704-9a5a-436cc0634195&info[name]=Postman Echo&info[description]=Postman Echo is service you can use to test your REST clients and make sample API calls. It provides endpoints for `GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, various auth mechanisms and other utility endpoints.

The documentation for the endpoints as well as example responses can be found at [https://postman-echo.com](https://postman-echo.com/?source=echo-collection-app-onboarding)&info[schema]=https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json&info[_exporter_id]=43864845&info[_collection_link]=https://www.postman.com/postman/published-postman-templates/collection/ucvy59g/postman-echo?action=share&source=collection_link&creator=43864845&item[0][name]=Request Methods&item[0][item][0][name]=GET Request&item[0][item][0][event][0][listen]=test&item[0][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=pm.test("response is ok", function () {&item[0][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=    pm.response.to.have.status(200);&item[0][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=});&item[0][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=&item[0][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=pm.test("response body has json with request queries", function () {&item[0][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=    pm.response.to.have.jsonBody('args.foo1', 'bar1')&item[0][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=        .and.have.jsonBody('args.foo2', 'bar2');&item[0][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=});&item[0][item][0][event][0][script][type]=text/javascript&item[0][item][0][request][method]=GET&item[0][item][0][request][url][raw]=https://postman-echo.com/get?foo1=bar1&foo2=bar2&item[0][item][0][request][url][protocol]=https&item[0][item][0][request][url][host][]=postman-echo&item[0][item][0][request][url][host][]=com&item[0][item][0][request][url][path][]=get&item[0][item][0][request][url][query][0][key]=foo1&item[0][item][0][request][url][query][0][value]=bar1&item[0][item][0][request][url][query][1][key]=foo2&item[0][item][0][request][url][query][1][value]=bar2&item[0][item][0][request][description]=The HTTP `GET` request method is meant to retrieve data from a server. The data
is identified by a unique URI (Uniform Resource Identifier).

A `GET` request can pass parameters to the server using "Query String
Parameters". For example, in the following request,

> http://example.com/hi/there?hand=wave

The parameter "hand" has the value "wave".

This endpoint echoes the HTTP headers, request parameters and the complete
URI requested.&item[0][item][0][response][0][name]=GET Request Woops&item[0][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][method]=GET&item[0][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][raw]=https://postman-echo.com/get?foo1=bar1&foo2=bar2&item[0][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][protocol]=https&item[0][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][host][]=postman-echo&item[0][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][host][]=com&item[0][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][path][]=get&item[0][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][query][0][key]=foo1&item[0][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][query][0][value]=bar1&item[0][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][query][1][key]=foo2&item[0][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][query][1][value]=bar2&item[0][item][0][response][0][status]=OK&item[0][item][0][response][0][code]=200&item[0][item][0][response][0][_postman_previewlanguage]=json&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][0][key]=Content-Encoding&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][0][value]=gzip&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][1][key]=Content-Type&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][1][value]=application/json; charset=utf-8&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][2][key]=Date&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][2][value]=Tue, 11 Jun 2019 10:43:13 GMT&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][3][key]=ETag&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][3][value]=W/"161-aLhNcsGArlgLSKbxPqfBW3viHPI"&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][4][key]=Server&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][4][value]=nginx&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][5][key]=set-cookie&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][5][value]=sails.sid=s%3AGz-wblZgXE8FCDq7aJpx_tUgZUcG3Nsw.LdNEN8L0C7nGWkvGLwvdw6R2s6Syjr%2FzkvyevA8qR0c; Path=/; HttpOnly&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][6][key]=Vary&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][6][value]=Accept-Encoding&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][7][key]=Content-Length&item[0][item][0][response][0][header][7][valu