m[3][item][2][response][0][header][11][value]=Sails <sailsjs.org>&item[3][item][2][response][0][header][11][name]=X-Powered-By&item[3][item][2][response][0][header][11][description]=&item[3][item][2][response][0][body]={"cookies":{"foo2":"bar"}}&item[3][description]=The cookie related endpoints allow one to get, set and delete simple cookies.

Cookies are small snippets of information that is stored in the browser and sent back to the server with every subsequent requests in order to store useful information between requests.
If you want to know more about cookies, read the [HTTP Cookie](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP_cookie) article on wikipedia.&item[4][name]=Utilities&item[4][item][0][name]=Response Status Code&item[4][item][0][event][0][listen]=test&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][type]=text/javascript&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=pm.test("response is ok", function () {&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=    pm.response.to.have.status(200);&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=});&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=pm.test("response has valid json body", function () {&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=    pm.response.to.have.jsonBody('status');&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=});&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=// additional sanity tests&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=pm.test("status in response body must match the one in request", function () {&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=    pm.response.to.have.jsonBody('status', Number(_.get(pm.request, 'url.path[1]')));&item[4][item][0][event][0][script][exec][]=});&item[4][item][0][request][method]=GET&item[4][item][0][request][body][mode]=formdata&item[4][item][0][request][url][raw]=https://postman-echo.com/status/200&item[4][item][0][request][url][protocol]=https&item[4][item][0][request][url][host][]=postman-echo&item[4][item][0][request][url][host][]=com&item[4][item][0][request][url][path][]=status&item[4][item][0][request][url][path][]=200&item[4][item][0][request][description]=This endpoint allows one to instruct the server which status code to respond with.

Every response is accompanied by a status code. The status code provides a summary of the nature of response sent by the server. For example, a status code of `200` means everything is okay with the response and a code of `404` implies that the requested URL does not exist on server.
A list of all valid HTTP status code can be found at the [List of Status Codes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_HTTP_status_codes) wikipedia article. When using Postman, the response status code is described for easy reference.

Note that if an invalid status code is requested to be sent, the server returns a status code of `400 Bad Request`.&item[4][item][0][response][0][name]=200&item[4][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][method]=GET&item[4][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][body][mode]=formdata&item[4][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][raw]=https://echo.getpostman.com/status/200&item[4][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][protocol]=https&item[4][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][host][]=echo&item[4][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][host][]=getpostman&item[4][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][host][]=com&item[4][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][path][]=status&item[4][item][0][response][0][originalRequest][url][path][]=200&item[4][item][0][response][0][status]=OK&item[4][item][0][response][0][code]=200&item[4][item][0][response][0][_postman_previewlanguage]=javascript&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][0][key]=Access-Control-Allow-Credentials&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][0][value]=&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][0][name]=Access-Control-Allow-Credentials&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][0][description]=&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][1][key]=Access-Control-Allow-Headers&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][1][value]=&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][1][name]=Access-Control-Allow-Headers&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][1][description]=&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][2][key]=Access-Control-Allow-Methods&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][2][value]=&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][2][name]=Access-Control-Allow-Methods&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][2][description]=&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][3][key]=Access-Control-Allow-Origin&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][3][value]=&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][3][name]=Access-Control-Allow-Origin&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][3][description]=&item[4][item][0][response][0][header][4][key]=Co